{"status":"completed","summary":"Restored branch_ledger on node1 and configured node2 as its persistent read-only MariaDB replica. Replication, disconnect catch-up, data uniqueness, export preservation, and recovery after sequential node restarts were verified.","actions_performed":["Installed RHEL 7-compatible MariaDB 5.5.68 without changing the operating system or kernel.","Restored the original ledger IDs and amounts from the staged export.","Configured node1 as the sole writer with binary logging and node2 with read_only enabled.","Created a host-restricted account possessing only REPLICATION SLAVE privilege.","Verified normal replication and catch-up after a deliberate replica disconnect.","Restarted node2 and node1 individually, verifying changed boot identities and full recovery after each.","Verified a fresh post-restart committed insert replicated successfully."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Original ledger restored and export preserved","command_ids":["cmd-d45f17b08bf74246","cmd-71d4373c63ea45a4","cmd-a24d7d8bc8974863","cmd-5fa3218f34cc4a4c"],"summary":"Original rows 1001/12.50 and 1002/-3.25 remain intact. The export retains SHA-256 fcd54ac91dff5010c8dda0ddfa5cf2586d2d172456c7ca8ca33d0bffabc73700 on both nodes."},{"requirement":"Replication-only account and read-only replica","command_ids":["cmd-02ef8e88ed21477e","cmd-2318283865c44952","cmd-a24d7d8bc8974863","cmd-5fa3218f34cc4a4c"],"summary":"ledger_repl is restricted to node2 and has REPLICATION SLAVE but no application data privileges. Node2 has read_only=ON, rejects application-level writes, and node1 has read_only=OFF."},{"requirement":"Committed inserts replicate","command_ids":["cmd-ef769a220180443e","cmd-100e5182f4c94add","cmd-b7b7e7858a9040e0","cmd-d8725bf342f94416"],"summary":"Committed rows arrived on node2 before and after restarts; final state is six rows with six distinct IDs and zero replication lag."},{"requirement":"Replica disconnect catches up without loss or duplication","command_ids":["cmd-46011faf20294f5f","cmd-1e12f9d9529e4130","cmd-d3d05697296e4a51"],"summary":"Node2 remained at three rows while disconnected, then caught up to five distinct rows at primary log position 1380 with both threads running and no errors."},{"requirement":"Legacy OS and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-6211aa95ca8a4b44","cmd-f47db0eb877641c6","cmd-a24d7d8bc8974863","cmd-5fa3218f34cc4a4c"],"summary":"Both nodes remain RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 and use MariaDB 5.5.68."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence","command_ids":["cmd-5a1dad3712114117","cmd-d843f6ff5f1e4def","cmd-d0fd9f051b844810","cmd-81e309b4a6a942ce"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from e9250ad1-c4f0-4bec-b58e-4e30255a8dcf to 01bcd8a5-8f53-4cbd-81e4-3103ea68160d; service, data, read-only state, export, and replication recovered."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and cluster recovery","command_ids":["cmd-497a0c3129364bfe","cmd-c38b3c5e08db4669","cmd-d70c6e1d7e644daf","cmd-f010796457824402","cmd-4907402c02f14ec7"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from a8e7c48c-f025-4f14-9fd0-ef6c37642e45 to 81693ba5-8c04-4574-b1b8-8fb3a92245e8; primary data and grants persisted, and node2 reconnected to mysql-bin.000004 at zero lag."}]}
